   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The inner expression is \\( u = 4 x^{2} - 17 \\), with \\( u' = 8 x \\), and \\( \\frac{d}{du}\\arctan u = \\frac{1}{1 + u^{2}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "inverse trigonometric derivative with the chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule and the chain rule, \\( h'(x) = \\frac{40 x^{2}}{\\left(4 x^{2} - 17\\right)^{2} + 1} + 5 \\arctan{\\left(4 x^{2} - 17 \\right)} \\).",
         "rule_named": "product rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At x = 2, \\( u = -1 \\) and \\( u' = 16 \\), so \\( h'(2) = - \\frac{5 \\pi}{4} + 80 = 80 - \\frac{5 \\pi}{4} \\).",
